@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# Plan
+
+1. Tighten the review request validation and endpoint status handling: use the path product id, reject non-whole ratings outside 1–5 with 400, enforce authenticated customer identity with 403, and report duplicate customer/product reviews as 409 before conversion or persistence.
+2. Replace the public review customer serialization with a minimal reviewer first-name field, preserving only the required review fields and preventing email/address/customer graph leakage.
+3. Make merchant update/delete lookup and product-scope failures consistently return 404, and ensure updates retain the requested review id.
+4. Centralize product aggregate recalculation in the product-review service by deriving count and one-decimal half-up average from the current persisted reviews after create, update, and delete; reset both fields to zero when no reviews remain.
+5. Add focused regression tests where practical, then run the relevant Maven tests and a full build, recording any environment limitations.
