+# Research
+
+## Request paths and DTOs
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/product/ProductReviewApi.java` owns the public GET and review POST/PUT/DELETE endpoints. The POST currently checks duplicate reviews with the body `productId` and `customerId`, overwrites the product id only afterward, returns 500 for duplicates and 503 for invalid ratings, and catches all failures as 503. The rating check only has an upper bound. PUT is exposed on both `/private` and `/auth`, checks the body customer id instead of merchant ownership, and uses a `reviewid` mapping with a `reviewId` parameter. DELETE checks the product relationship but delegates deletion without recalculating product aggregates.
+- `sm-shop-model/.../ProductReviewEntity.java` has `@Min(1)`/`@Max(5)` on a `Double`, which allows fractional values and relies on exception handling for malformed requests. `PersistableProductReview` adds `customerId`.
+- `ReadableProductReview` currently contains a `ReadableCustomer customer` property. The catalog `ReadableProductReviewPopulator` calls `ReadableCustomerPopulator`, which fills the customer email, billing/delivery addresses and other fields; this is the source of the public privacy leak.
+
+## Persistence and rating behavior
+
+- `ProductReview` has a database unique constraint on `(CUSTOMERS_ID, PRODUCT_ID)`, plus customer/product relationships and descriptions.
+- `ProductReviewRepository.findByProductAndCustomer` provides the existing duplicate lookup. Its product list queries eagerly fetch the customer graph, so the public mapping must explicitly project only the approved reviewer field.
+- `ProductReviewServiceImpl.saveOrUpdate` reads the product's stored average/count, always adds the incoming rating and increments the count, then saves. Therefore updates are counted as new reviews and can produce incorrect ratings. It does not validate the rating as an integer in range, does not prevent cross-product update use, and does not override the product aggregates after deletion.
+- `ProductCommonFacadeImpl` converts request DTOs through `PersistableProductReviewPopulator`, then calls `create` or `update`; `deleteReview` only calls `productReviewService.delete`.
+- Product response mappers (`ReadableProductMapper`, `ReadableProductDefinitionMapper`, `ReadableMinimalProductMapper`) expose `productReviewAvg`/`productReviewCount` as `rating`/`ratingCount`, including the v2 product response. Product model fields are `BigDecimal productReviewAvg` and `Integer productReviewCount`.
+
+## Authentication and affected behavior
+
+- Customer JWT authentication supplies a `JWTUser` principal with `getId()`. Existing APIs obtain it through `HttpServletRequest.getUserPrincipal()`. The review POST must compare this authenticated id with the submitted `customerId` and return 403 before any persistence.
+- The requested one-review rule is already represented in the entity/database constraint and lookup, but the endpoint currently reports the duplicate as a server error. It must return 409 and perform all refusal checks before conversion/save.
+- Merchant review PUT/DELETE must identify the review by id and verify its product id; a missing review or wrong product must be 404. Merchant authorization is already provided by the endpoint security configuration, so no customer-id ownership check should be used for these merchant operations.
+
+## Tests/build impact
+
+- Existing integration coverage is in `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/product/ProductManagementAPIIntegrationTest.java`, including private review creation. Relevant new coverage should target public response fields, POST statuses/validation/no-write behavior, merchant update/delete product scoping, and aggregate recalculation after create/update/delete/empty state.
+- The repository is a multi-module Maven build with root modules `sm-core-model`, `sm-core-modules`, `sm-core`, `sm-shop-model`, and `sm-shop`; Java 21 is available although the POM targets Java 11.
